otocol (cmd-d8a4f171fbd54943). Other commands were read-only observations. Post-execution snapshots show no failed services, damaged package state, new exposure, or abandoned temporary residue; socket and systemd-private path differences are normal consequences of the verified reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7a2e2a190cbc4af8","cmd-6494d5b9334d4b4d","cmd-d8a4f171fbd54943","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the connection disruption was observed, the boot ID changed, and the system, timer, policy, active log, and compressed archive recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The evidence validates the seven-archive retention setting through logrotate's parser and one real compressed rotation; it does not exercise eight successive rotations to observe oldest-archive eviction.","Daily eligibility is directly shown by the parsed policy and active scheduler, but the short evidence window does not include a naturally timed next-day rotation."]}
